### AI Fabric Runtime — local smoke requests
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8097
@trustedBackendApiKey = change-me
@userId = user-1
@sessionId = user-1-session
@conversationId = chat-user-1

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### Swagger UI (open in browser)
# {{baseUrl}}/swagger-ui/index.html

### Chat: query using verified auth context (preferred secure contract)
# Response headers should include:
# - X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-AUTH-MODE
# - X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-COMPATIBILITY-IDENTITY
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/query
Content-Type: application/json
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

{
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "query": "What can you do?"
}

### Chat: suggestions using verified auth context
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/suggestions
Content-Type: application/json
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

{
  "content": "I want to search my docs",
  "maxSuggestions": 5
}

### Auth context using verified runtime identity
# Useful for integration smoke tests and for checking the effective runtime caller identity.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/auth-context
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

### Conversations using verified auth context (requires ai.chat.enabled=true)
# Use the auth-aware /me surface for verified callers.
# These endpoints require verified runtime auth context and reject request userId/sessionId/ownerId hints.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/conversations
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

### Conversation detail using verified auth context
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/conversations/{{conversationId}}
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

### Delete conversation using verified auth context
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/conversations/{{conversationId}}
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-ID: {{userId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SUBJECT-TYPE: END_USER
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-MODE: PRIVATE_RUNTIME_BACKEND_MEDIATED
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-CALLER-TYPE: TRUSTED_BACKEND
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-SESSION-ID: {{sessionId}}
X-AIFABRIC-AUTH-ISSUER: runtime.http

### Legacy compatibility chat query (migration-only)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/query
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}",
  "conversationId": "{{conversationId}}",
  "query": "What can you do?"
}

### Legacy compatibility conversations (migration-only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/conversations?ownerId={{userId}}

### Legacy compatibility auth context (migration-only)
# This endpoint remains available only to help migration off request identity fields.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/auth-context?userId={{userId}}&sessionId={{sessionId}}

### Public runtime anonymous bootstrap (opt-in mode)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/public/chat/session
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: https://shop.example

{
  "sessionId": "anon-runtime-http"
}

### Public runtime anonymous chat query (paste token from bootstrap response)
@publicRuntimeToken = paste-token-here
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/query
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{publicRuntimeToken}}

{
  "conversationId": "chat-anon-runtime-http",
  "query": "What can you do for an anonymous shopper?"
}

### Public runtime anonymous conversations
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/chat/me/conversations
Authorization: Bearer {{publicRuntimeToken}}

### Data Sync: list vector spaces (requires embeddings enabled + data sync enabled)
# Add the trusted backend API key when runtime ingress is configured for strict backend-only operational surfaces.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ai/data-sync/vector-spaces
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}

### Data Sync: upsert a document into vector space "document"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ai/data-sync/upsert
Content-Type: application/json
X-AIFABRIC-RUNTIME-API-KEY: {{trustedBackendApiKey}}

{
  "vectorSpace": "document",
  "id": "doc-1",
  "content": "Return policy: returns accepted within 30 days with receipt.",
  "metadata": { "source": "runtime.http" },
  "trace": { "requestId": "req-1", "userId": "{{userId}}", "sessionId": "{{sessionId}}" }
}
